course: dictionary
lesson: 12018
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is right. Chine is a rare word with several meanings. The sentences around it are your clues.
explain: «The stream ran down the chine, between tall cliffs, to the sea.» The clues are stream, cliffs and sea. A chine here is a deep, narrow valley cut by water, not a bone.
explain: «The butcher chined the lamb before he carved it.» The clues are butcher, lamb and carved. Here chine is a cooking word, meaning to cut through the backbone of meat so it is easier to carve.
explain: Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Swap your meaning in and check that the sentence still makes sense. If it does not, try the next meaning.
fact: Chine has several meanings: the backbone of an animal, a ridge of land, a deep narrow valley, and a cooking verb.
fact: As a noun, «chine» can mean a joint of meat that includes part of the backbone.
fact: On the south coast of England, a chine is a deep, narrow ravine cut by a stream through soft cliffs to the sea, as in Blackgang Chine on the Isle of Wight.
fact: As a verb, «chined» and «chining» are about cooking: cutting through the backbone of a joint of meat.
fact: A ridge is a long, narrow line of high land, like the top of a mountain.
exercise: «The stream ran down the chine to the sea, between tall, crumbling cliffs.» What is a chine here? | A short, rude reply | A bone in a fish | A kind of hat | *A deep, narrow valley cut by water
exercise: «The cook chined the joint before roasting it.» What does chine mean here? | To wrap the meat in foil | To sing while cooking | *To cut through the backbone of meat | To wash the meat in cold water
exercise: «The goat walked along the chine, a narrow ridge high above the valley.» What is a chine here? | A soft, sandy beach | *A narrow ridge of land | A deep pond | A type of goat
test: «The lamb was chined by the butcher.» What does chine mean here? | *To cut through the backbone | To cook slowly for hours | To put in a box
test: «The hikers followed the chine down to the beach, past the waterfall.» What is a chine here? | A tall tree | *A deep, narrow ravine cut by a stream | A wooden bridge | A small village
exam: «Blackgang Chine is a famous place on the Isle of Wight.» What is a chine here? | *A deep, narrow ravine cut by a stream to the sea | A large island | A famous castle | A sort of boat
